Subject: [PATCH] Fix the top utility-rail icons doing nothing on mobile
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TopNav's 6-icon rail (Calendar/Teammates/Notifications/Autopilot/
Upcoming/Plan) is rendered on every dashboard page, unconditionally
visible on all viewport widths. Its target, RightUtilityPanel, is a
compact side panel with a drag-to-resize rail — it only ever renders
`hidden md:flex`, deliberately desktop-only, since a side panel has no
sensible shape on a narrow viewport. Below the md breakpoint, tapping
any of the 6 icons still fired onSelect(key) and set activePanel, just
with nowhere visible for that state to show up — a tap "worked" and
produced zero visible result, indistinguishable from the button being
dead.

Fix: on mobile, each icon now navigates straight to that panel's own
real full-screen page instead (RIGHT_PANEL_META's expandHref) — the
exact same destination the desktop panel's own "Expand" button already
uses, not a new surface. Desktop keeps the original compact-panel
button row untouched, just now explicitly `hidden md:flex` instead of
always-rendered-but-silently-broken below it.

Swept the rest of the app for the same "always-visible trigger wired
to a hidden md: target" pattern (global-search.tsx, live-execution-
feed.tsx) — both hits there are responsive text/hint elements, not
broken triggers, so this looks like the one real instance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
